  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.1.0: your own fonts and more languages. Load .ttf and .otf fonts (including variable fonts) with PdfFont and draw Hindi, Telugu, Tamil, and Latin-script text, shaped by the font's rules, on every text call and in HTML; fallback fonts per character; FindMissingCharacters and FailOnMissingCharacters; PDFs embed only the glyphs they use, and copied text reads back as written. Extract or remove pages of a PDF in one call with PdfOperations.Extract and Remove, keeping only the fonts and images those pages use; PdfPageRange.Parse reads page lists such as 2, 5, 7-9, and PdfDocument.AddPages takes page ranges (a positional null page number, as in AddPages(file, null, 7), now needs its name). Text without a font now draws Western European characters such as é and € instead of ?. Fixes: table numbers are never written in exponent form, and damaged PDFs loaded to merge or split are refused quickly. https://github.com/unlimited-docs/UnlimitedPDF#changes-in-110 — 1.0.1: text now shows in iPhone and iPad PDF viewers. Every page names the font its text uses; pages look the same everywhere else, and the API is unchanged. https://github.com/unlimited-docs/UnlimitedPDF#changes-in-101 — 1.0.0: merge PDFs, split PDFs, and HTML to PDF with a built-in renderer; tables that continue across pages with repeated header rows; headers, footers, page numbers, and a body flow that adds pages as needed; JPEG and PNG images, also in table cells; colors from RGB or hex; .NET 11 support. Part of the API is renamed, so code written for 0.0.x needs the new names. The full change list and the upgrade table: https://github.com/unlimited-docs/UnlimitedPDF#changes-in-100",
